    "https://www.moval.edu/about/careers-at-mvc/": {
      "title": "Director of Admissions",
      "description": "Employment Opportunities - Missouri Valley University Skip to content Missouri Valley University Menu About About Mission, Vision, Values, and Goals God, Family, Country Our History Consumer Information Offices Leadership Careers at MVC Morris Gallery of Contemporary Art Faces of Jesus Exhibit Campus & Directions Meet Our Students & Alumni Admissions & Financial Aid Admissions & Financial Aid How to Apply Tuition & Financial Aid Scholarships Visit Missouri Valley International Students New Student Orientation Meet Our Admissions Team Payments/Policies 1098-T Information Student Employment Program Parent Resources Academics Academics Programs of Study Academic Schools Course Offerings Learning Beyond the Classroom New Student Orientation Honors College Graduate Studies MVU Online Dual Credit for High School Students Murrell Library and Academic Support Center Academic Calendar Academic Catalog Faculty Teaching Award Recipients Graduation Information Institutional Review Board Certificate Programs Student Engagement Student Engagement Activities & Events Clubs & Organizations Recreation & Fitness New Student Orientation Student Handbook Housing & Dining Health & Wellness Getting Out & About Campus Chaplain Student Employment Safety & Security Accessibility & Disability Services Student Success Center Title IX News & Events News & Events News Events Publications Social Media Alumni Alumni Homecoming Stay Connected Outstanding Alumni Alumni Recognition Center and Museum Athletic Hall of Fame Nomination Alumni Events Alumni Advisory Board Legacy Scholarship Transcript Request Viking Views Magazine Giving Viking Tailgate Zone Viking Apparel Store Athletics Search Search Search for: MyMoval Faculty & Staff Directory Pay Enrollment Fee Give to MVU Section Navigation Employment Opportunities Director of Athletics Head STUNT Coach Adjunct and Graduate Assistant Positions Head Cheer Coach Missouri Valley University | About | Employment Opportunities Employment Opportunities Join a Vibrant Liberal Arts College Here at Valley, we are always looking for qualified and exceptional faculty and staff to join our campus community. Check out some of our openings, and see if Valley is the right fit for your career needs! Missouri Valley College is an Equal Opportunity Employer and adheres to the Civil Rights Act of 1964, as amended, the Americans with Disabilities Act of 1990, and other legislation prohibiting discrimination in employment and access to educational programs. Employment decisions are made based on qualifications, merit, and business needs. We are committed to fostering a diverse and inclusive environment, and all eligible candidates are encouraged to apply. Adjunct and Graduate Assistant Positions Printable Application Director of Admissions Director of Admissions Location: Marshall, Missouri FLSA Status: Exempt Open Date: June 5, 2026 Closing Date: Open until filled Missouri Valley College (MVC) invites applications for Director of Admissions. This dynamic and strategic leader will serve as the College’s chief enrollment strategist, developing and implementing innovative recruitment and enrollment management initiatives that drive sustainable enrollment growth, enhance student success, and support the long-term financial health of the institution. Key Responsibilities Develop and execute a comprehensive multi-year enrollment growth strategy aligned with institutional goals, demographic trends, and market opportunities. Identify, evaluate, and expand new recruitment markets, including out-of-state, transfer, adult learner, online, military-affiliated, and international student populations. Partner with Marketing and Communications to strengthen the College’s brand awareness, digital recruitment efforts, and lead-generation campaigns. Establish enrollment goals, key performance indicators (KPIs), and forecasting models; regularly assess progress and adjust strategies to maximize enrollment outcomes. Lead competitive market analysis and environmental scanning to identify emerging opportunities, enrollment risks, and program demand trends. Collaborate with Academic Affairs to develop and promote academic programs that align with workforce needs and student demand. Strengthen relationships with high schools, community colleges, workforce development organizations, counselors, coaches, alumni, and community partners to expand recruitment pipelines. Develop and oversee strategic scholarship leveraging and financial aid recruitment initiatives in partnership with Financial Aid to optimize enrollment yield and net tuition revenue. Utilize technology, automation, and CRM best practices to improve prospect engagement, communication effectiveness, and conversion rates throughout the enrollment funnel. Represent the College at regional, state, and national enrollment management organizations, conferences, and community events to advance institutional visibility and partnerships. Provide regular enrollment reports, projections, and strategic recommendations to senior leadership to support institutional planning and resource allocation. Foster a culture of continuous improvement by implementing innovative recruitment practices, evaluating outcomes, and scaling successful initiatives. Lead, mentor, and evaluate Admissions staff, promoting a culture of service and accountability in support of the MVC Mission. Qualifications Bachelor’s degree; master’s degree preferred. Previous experience as an Assistant or Associate Director of Admissions. Demonstrated success in recruitment or enrollment growth. Strong analytical and organizational skills, including experience using CRM systems, databases, or enrollment management tools. Excellent communication, presentation, and interpersonal skills. Application Instructions To apply, please email cover letter, resume, and contact information for three professional references to HR@moval.edu . References will not be contacted without prior knowledge and approval of candidates. Additional Information As a pre-condition of employment, applicants must be authorized to work in the United States. Employment at Missouri Valley College is contingent upon satisfactory completion of a background check. Salary commensurate with education and experience. A comprehensive benefit package is available which includes medical, vision, and dental insurance; flexible spending; life insurance; retirement; holidays; and sick days. Occasional evening and weekend work may be required. May require occasional overnight travel. Equal Opportunity Employer Missouri Valley College is an Equal Opportunity Employer and adheres to the Civil Rights Act of 1964, as amended, the Americans with Disabilities Act of 1990, and other legislation prohibiting discrimination in employment and access to educational programs. Employment decisions are made based on qualifications, merit, and business needs, and all eligible candidates are encouraged to apply. Controller Controller Location: Remote or Marshall, MO. FLSA Status: Exempt Reports To: Vice-President of Business & Finance Open Date: Immediately Closing Date: Open until filled Missouri Valley University invites applications for a Controller to provide leadership and oversight of the University’s financial operations. The Controller is responsible for ensuring accurate and timely financial reporting, maintaining strong internal controls, overseeing accounting functions, and supporting the University’s long-term financial sustainability. Working collaboratively with the Vice President of Business and Finance and other University leaders, the Controller helps advance MVU’s mission through sound fiscal management, regulatory compliance, effective financial processes, and responsive support for departments across the institution. This position may be performed remotely or on campus in Marshall, Missouri, depending on the qualifications and circumstances of the successful candidate. Primary Responsibilities Direct all accounting operations, including general ledger, accounts payable, accounts receivable, fixed assets, payroll accounting, grants accounting, Information Technology, Financial Aid, Human Resources, and cash management. Prepare, analyze, and present timely monthly, quarterly, and annual financial statements. Ensure compliance with Generally Accepted Accounting Principles (GAAP), federal and state regulations, and higher-education accounting standards. Coordinate and prepare year-end audit schedules; serve as primary liaison to external auditors. Budgeting & Forecasting Support the VP of Business and Finance in developing the annual operating and capital budgets. Provide financial modeling, forecasting, and trend analysis to guide decision-making. Monitor budget performance and provide periodic variance reporting to campus leaders. Compliance & Internal Controls Develop, implement, and maintain effective internal controls and financial policies. Ensure compliance with federal and state regulatory requirements, including IRS, U.S. Department of Education, and grant-specific guidelines. Oversee proper accounting treatment for restricted funds, endowment activity, and donor-designated contributions. Leadership & Collaboration Supervise and mentor accounting staff, fostering a culture of accuracy, accountability, and professional development. Collaborate with academic and administrative departments to support financial processes and improve service delivery. Partner with the Office of Financial Aid to support federal financial aid compliance, Title IV requirements, and reconciliation processes. Operational Oversight Manage cash flow, banking activities, and investment accounting. Oversee implementation and maintenance of financial systems and technology. Evaluate and enhance accounting procedures to increase efficiency and accuracy. Minimum Qualifications Bachelor’s degree in Accounting, Finance, Business Administration, or related field. Minimum of 3-5 years of progressive accounting experience. Strong knowledge of GAAP and nonprofit/higher-education accounting practices. Demonstrated experience preparing financial statements and leading audits. Proven leadership, supervisory, and communication skills. Preferred Qualifications Certified Public Accountant (CPA). Master’s degree in Accounting/Finance. Experience in higher education, nonprofit organizations, or fund accounting. Familiarity with ERP systems (e.g., Jenzabar, Ellucian, or similar platforms). Application Instructions To apply, please email cover letter, curriculum vitae, and three professional references to hr@moval.edu . References will not be contacted without prior knowledge and approval of candidates. Additional Information As a pre-condition of employment, the applicant must be authorized to work in the United States. Employment at MVC is contingent upon successful completion of reference and background checks. Salary commensurate with education and experience. A comprehensive benefit package is available which includes medical, vision, and dental insurance; flexible spending; life insurance; retirement; holidays; sick days. Equal Opportunity Employer Missouri Valley University is an Equal Opportunity Employer and committed to a diverse and inclusive environment. Missouri Valley University does not discriminate on the grounds of color, race, sex, religion, marital status, disability, national origin, veteran’s status, age, or sexual orientation. Employment decisions are based on qualifications, merit, and business needs. All eligible candidates are encouraged to apply. Head Track & Field Coach Missouri Valley College seeks an energetic, visionary, and student-centered Head Track & Field Coach to provide leadership for the College’s men’s and women’s track & field programs. The Head Coach is responsible for all aspects of program administration, including recruiting, roster management, coaching, player development, academic success, budgeting, scheduling, fundraising, alumni engagement, and compliance with institutional, conference, and NAIA regulations. The successful candidate will foster a culture of competitive excellence, integrity, sportsmanship, academic achievement, and personal development while supporting the mission and values of Missouri Valley College. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Program Leadership Provide strategic leadership and long-term vision for the men’s and women’s track & field programs. Develop a competitive program capable of contending for conference championships and national qualification. Establish a positive, disciplined, and inclusive team culture. Promote sportsmanship, leadership, accountability, and character development among student-athletes. Develop annual goals and measurable objectives for team and individual success. Hire, supervise, and evaluate assistant coaches and support staff Coaching Responsibilities Plan, organize, and conduct all phases of the program to include but not limited to practices and conditioning sessions. Develop individualized training plans for distance, middle-distance, sprint, hurdle, jump, throw, and multis athletes. Coach during all practices and competitions. Evaluate athlete performance using data, video analysis, and performance metrics. Coordinate strength and conditioning programs in collaboration with athletic performance staff. Work closely with athletic training personnel regarding injury prevention and rehabilitation. Recruiting Recruit and retain qualified student-athletes who align with Missouri Valley College’s academic and athletic standards. Develop and maintain recruiting territories and pipelines throughout Missouri and nationally. Conduct campus visits, recruiting communications, evaluations, and scholarship recommendations. Build strong relationships with high school coaches, club coaches, and community college programs. Utilize recruiting software and databases effectively. Student-Athlete Development Foster a positive team culture emphasizing sportsmanship, discipline, and personal growth Monitor academic progress and encourage timely degree completion. Support student-athlete retention, leadership development, and overall well-being. Work collaboratively with academic support services. Promote life skills, career readiness, and community involvement. Compliance Ensure full compliance with: NAIA rules and regulations Heart of America Athletic Conference policies Missouri Valley College policies Title IX requirements Institutional eligibility standards Maintain required documentation and certifications. Participate in compliance education and reporting. Program Administration Prepare and manage annual operating budgets. Coordinate team travel, lodging, meals, and transportation. Schedule competitions in collaboration with the Director of Athletics. Manage equipment purchasing, inventory, and maintenance. Coordinate facility usage and practice schedules. Supervise assistant coaches, graduate assistants, volunteer coaches, and student workers. Fundraising and Community Engagement Assist with athletic department fundraising initiatives. Develop relationships with alumni, donors, and community supporters. Participate in admissions and enrollment events. Conduct youth camps and clinics. Represent Missouri Valley College at community functions and professional organizations. Administrative Responsibilities Maintain accurate statistical records. Complete required reports and evaluations. Participate in departmental meetings and professional development. Assist with game management and other departmental responsibilities as assigned. Support the overall mission and strategic goals of the athletics department. Required Qualifications Bachelor’s degree from an accredited institution. Previous collegiate coaching and/or recruiting experience. Demonstrated knowledge of training methodologies. Strong organizational, leadership, and communication skills. Ability to recruit and retain high-quality student-athletes. Working knowledge of NAIA rules and eligibility standards. Valid driver’s license with acceptable driving record. Ability to travel extensively and work evenings, weekends, and holidays as required. Preferred Qualifications Master’s degree. Head coaching experience at the collegiate level. Experience coaching multiple event disciplines. Successful history of recruiting and retaining student-athletes. Experience managing operating budgets. Demonstrated fundraising and alumni engagement success. Experience using recruiting software, performance analytics, and meet management systems. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities The successful candidate will demonstrate: Exceptional leadership and mentoring abilities. Strong interpersonal and relationship-building skills. Effective verbal and written communication. Organizational and time-management excellence. Strategic planning and program development. Ability to work collaboratively across campus. Strong decision-making and problem-solving skills. High ethical standards and professional integrity. Physical Requirements Ability to stand and walk for extended periods. Ability to demonstrate athletic skills and training techniques. Ability to lift and move equipment weighing up to 50 pounds. Ability to travel frequently by automobile and commercial transportation. Ability to work outdoors in varying weather conditions. Working Conditions Evening and weekend work is required. Extensive seasonal travel. Indoor and outdoor coaching environments. Occasional overnight travel. Fast-paced athletic environment requiring flexibility and adaptability. Performance Expectations The Head Coach will be evaluated based upon: Competitive success Student-athlete retention Academic achievement Graduation rates Recruiting effectiveness Compliance with NAIA and institutional policies Budget management Fundraising and community engagement Leadership and staff supervision Contribution to the mission of Missouri Valley College Application Instructions To apply, please email cover letter, curriculum vitae, and three professional references to hr@moval.edu . References will not be contacted without prior knowledge and approval of candidates. Additional Information As a pre-condition of employment, the applicant must be authorized to work in the United States. Employment at MVC is contingent upon successful completion of reference and background checks. Salary commensurate with education and experience. A comprehensive benefit package is available which includes medical, vision, and dental insurance; flexible spending; life insurance; retirement; holidays; sick days. Equal Opportunity Employer Missouri Valley College is an Equal Opportunity Employer and committed to a diverse and inclusive environment. Missouri Valley College does not discriminate on the grounds of color, race, sex, religion, marital status, disability, national origin, veteran’s status, age, or sexual orientation. Employment decisions are based on qualifications, merit, and business needs. All eligible candidates are encouraged to apply. Rodeo Assistant Coach Position Summary: The Rodeo Assistant Coach will work closely with the Head Coach to support the development and success of the rodeo team. This role includes responsibilities in recruitment, fundraising, and assisting with the Future Farmers of America (FFA) program, as well as ensuring the eligibility of team members. Salary: $40,000 per year Estimated Start Date: August/ September 2026 Key Responsibilities: Recruiting: Identify and recruit prospective student-athletes interested in joining the rodeo team. Attend rodeo events, high school competitions, and fairs to scout talent. Maintain relationships with local high schools, rodeo associations, and community organizations. Fundraising: Collaborate with the head coach to create and implement fundraising strategies and campaigns to support the rodeo program. Organize fundraising events, sponsorships, and outreach to local businesses and community members. Manage donations and funding arrangements for team activities, travel, and equipment needs. FFA Support and Engagement: Assist the FFA program by providing coaching and mentoring to members interested in rodeo events. Promote the rodeo team’s involvement in FFA activities and competitions. – Collaborate with FFA advisors to facilitate training sessions and workshops. Eligibility and Compliance: Ensure all team members meet eligibility requirements and maintain compliance with league and school regulations. Assist in the academic monitoring of athletes and promote academic success and responsibility. Coaching and Training: Support the Head Coach in organizing practices and training sessions for the team. – Work individually with athletes to enhance their skills and performance in rodeo events. – Provide guidance on techniques, safety, and sportsmanship. Team Administration: Assist with managing team schedules, travel arrangements, and logistics. – Maintain accurate records of team activities, athlete performance, and academic progress. Communicate regularly with athletes and their families regarding schedules, expectations, and progress. Qualifications: High School Diploma or equivalent; Bachelor’s degree in a relevant field is a plus. Experience in competitive rodeo as a participant or coach. Strong communication and interpersonal skills. Ability to work collaboratively with coaches, athletes, and community members. Passion for supporting student-athletes and promoting the sport of rodeo. Preferred Skills: Familiarity with FFA and its programs. Fundraising experience and event planning skills. Knowledge of eligibility regulations and compliance requirements. Application Process: To apply, please email cover letter, resume, and contact information for three professional references to HR@moval.edu. References will not be contacted without prior knowledge and approval of candidates. Additional Information As a pre-condition of employment, the applicant must be authorized to work in the United States. Employment at MVC is contingent upon satisfactory completion of background check. Salary commensurate with education and experience. A comprehensive benefit package is available which includes medical, vision, and dental insurance; flexible spending; life insurance; retirement; holidays; sick days. Equal Opportunity Employer Missouri Valley College is an Equal Opportunity Employer and committed to a diverse and inclusive environment. Missouri Valley College does not discriminate on the grounds of color, race, sex, religion, or marital status, disability, national origin, veteran’s status, age, or sexual orientation. Employment decisions are based on qualifications, merit, and business needs. All eligible candidates are encouraged to apply. About Missouri Valley College Founded in 1889, Missouri Valley College is a private, four-year liberal arts institution located in Marshall, Missouri. Known for its diverse and student-focused environment, MVC provides an engaging educational experience that prepares graduates for meaningful careers and lifelong learning. Through innovative teaching and interdisciplinary learning, MVC empowers students to succeed in a knowledge-driven global society. Admissions Representative - Main Campus Job Summary: The Admissions Representative is an integral part of the admissions team, responsible for promoting Missouri Valley College and supporting prospective students through the admissions process. This position will focus on effectively managing CRM communications to enhance the overall applicant experience, with a particular emphasis on coordinating and facilitating dual credit program inquiries, providing graduate student advising, and undertaking additional duties as assigned. Key Responsibilities: Serve as a key contact for prospective students, parents, and educational partners regarding admissions inquiries for graduate and dual credit programs. Provide advising and guidance to prospective graduate students on program offerings, admission requirements, and career opportunities. Assist with the development and implementation of recruitment strategies to attract potential students to the college. Guide students through the application process, ensuring they understand admission requirements and timelines. Review and evaluate applications for admission, providing recommendations based on established criteria. Coordinate and participate in outreach activities, including information sessions, college fairs, and community events. Collaborate with academic departments to maintain up-to-date information on program offerings and admission criteria. Assist in the creation and distribution of recruitment materials and communication strategies tailored to diverse audiences. Maintain detailed records of prospective students and admissions activities in the college’s database. Work closely with the Director and Assistant Director of Admissions to develop and enhance admissions procedures. Perform additional duties as assigned by the Director or Assistant Director of Admissions. Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree in education, marketing, communication, or a related field preferred. Previous experience in admissions, recruitment, or higher education is advantageous. Excellent interpersonal, communication, and problem-solving skills. Strong organizational skills with the ability to manage multiple tasks simultaneously. Proficiency in Microsoft Office and experience with student information systems preferred. Ability to work collaboratively with diverse populations. Application Process: To apply, please email cover letter, resume, and contact information for three professional references to HR@moval.edu. References will not be contacted without prior knowledge and approval of candidates. Additional Information As a pre-condition of employment, the applicant must be authorized to work in the United States. Employment at MVC is contingent upon satisfactory completion of background check. Salary commensurate with education and experience. A comprehensive benefit package is available which includes medical, vision, and dental insurance; flexible spending; life insurance; retirement; holidays; sick days. Equal Opportunity Employer Missouri Valley College is an Equal Opportunity Employer and committed to a diverse and inclusive environment. Missouri Valley College does not discriminate on the grounds of color, race, sex, religion, or marital status, disability, national origin, veteran’s status, age, or sexual orientation. Employment decisions are based on qualifications, merit, and business needs. All eligible candidates are encouraged to apply. About Missouri Valley College Founded in 1889, Missouri Valley College is a private, four-year liberal arts institution located in Marshall, Missouri. Known for its diverse and student-focused environment, MVC provides an engaging educational experience that prepares graduates for meaningful careers and lifelong learning. Through innovative teaching and interdisciplinary learning, MVC empowers students to succeed in a knowledge-driven global society. Head Softball Coach Missouri Valley College invites applications for the position of Head Softball Coach. This is a full-time position responsible for leading and growing a competitive intercollegiate softball program that aligns with the College’s mission of academic excellence, character development, and student success. The Head Coach will oversee all aspects of the softball program, including recruiting, player development, academic success, and program administration. The successful candidate will demonstrate strong leadership, integrity, and a commitment to building a championship-caliber program both on and off the field. Key Responsibilities Plan, organize, and direct all phases of the softball program Recruit and retain qualified student-athletes who align with Missouri Valley College’s mission Develop and implement effective training, practice, and competition strategies Monitor academic progress and promote student-athlete success in the classroom Manage program budget, scheduling, and travel Hire, supervise, and evaluate assistant coaches and support staff Ensure compliance with NAIA and conference rules and regulations Foster a positive team culture emphasizing sportsmanship, discipline, and personal growth Engage in fundraising, alumni relations, and community outreach efforts Qualifications Bachelor’s degree required; Master’s degree preferred Previous coaching experience at the collegiate level (head coaching experience preferred) Strong knowledge of softball skills, strategy, and player development Demonstrated success in recruiting student-athletes Excellent communication, organizational, and leadership skills Commitment to compliance with institutional, conference, and NAIA rules Ability to work evenings, weekends, and travel as required Application Instructions To apply, please email cover letter, resume, and three professional references to hr@moval.edu . Additional Information As a pre-condition of employment, the applicant must be authorized to work in the United States. Employment at MVC is contingent upon satisfactory completion of background check. Salary commensurate with education and experience. A comprehensive benefit package is available which includes medical, vision, and dental insurance; flexible spending; life insurance; retirement; holidays; sick days. Equal Opportunity Employer Missouri Valley College is an Equal Opportunity Employer and committed to a diverse and inclusive environment. Missouri Valley College does not discriminate on the grounds of color, race, sex, religion, marital status, disability, national origin, veteran’s status, age, or sexual orientation. Employment decisions are based on qualifications, merit, and business needs. All eligible candidates are encouraged to apply. About Missouri Valley College Founded in 1889, Missouri Valley College is a private, four-year liberal arts institution located in Marshall, Missouri. Known for its diverse and student-focused environment, MVC provides an engaging educational experience that prepares graduates for meaningful careers and lifelong learning. Head Cheer Coach Missouri Valley College seeks a talented, hard-working leader to serve as its next cheer coach. The coach is responsible for leading and developing a competitive and game-day cheer program within the NAIA, UCA, and NCA. The coach promotes student-athlete success academically, athletically, and personally while representing the institution with professionalism and integrity. The coach will plan, organize, and direct all aspects of the cheer program, teaching and supervising stunts, choreography, sideline and competition routines, fostering a disciplined team culture and ensuring safety through proper training and risk management. Key Responsibilities Plan, organize, and direct all aspects of the cheer program. Meet or exceed institutional recruitment goals while Identifying, evaluating, and recruiting prospective student-athletes aligned with institutional and NAIA standards. Build relationships with high school and club cheer programs. Assist recruits through admissions and financial aid processes. Support retention and academic success of current team members Coordinate cheer participation at football, basketball, and other athletic events. Maintain compliance with NAIA and NCA rules, eligibility standards, and institutional policies. Manage team budget, travel, uniforms, and equipment. Schedule practices, competitions, and travel logistics. Required Qualifications Bachelor’s degree (required); Master’s preferred. Collegiate cheerleading and/or coaching experience. Knowledge of stunt safety, tumbling progression, and choreography. Strong leadership, communication, and organizational skills. Ability to recruit and retain student-athletes. CPR/AED and First Aid certification (or ability to obtain) Knowledge of NAIA rules and recruiting practices. Strong social media and program promotion skills. Evening and weekend travel required Ability to lift, spot, and demonstrate cheer techniques safely. Application Instructions To apply, please email cover letter, curriculum vitae, and references to hr@moval.edu . References will not be contacted without prior knowledge and approval of candidates. Additional Information As a pre-condition of employment, the applicant must be authorized to work in the United States. Employment at MVC is contingent upon satisfactory completion of background check. Salary commensurate with education and experience. A comprehensive benefit package is available which includes medical, vision, and dental insurance; flexible spending; life insurance; retirement; holidays; sick days. Equal Opportunity Employer Missouri Valley College is an Equal Opportunity Employer and committed to a diverse and inclusive environment. Missouri Valley College does not discriminate on the grounds of color, race, sex, religion, marital status, disability, national origin, veteran’s status, age, or sexual orientation. Employment decisions are based on qualifications, merit, and business needs. All eligible candidates are encouraged to apply. About Missouri Valley College Founded in 1889, Missouri Valley College is a private, four-year liberal arts institution located in Marshall, Missouri. Known for its diverse and student-focused environment, MVC provides an engaging educational experience that prepares graduates for meaningful careers and lifelong learning. Through innovative teaching and interdisciplinary learning, MVC empowers students to succeed in a knowledge-driven global society Althletic Trainer Missouri Valley College has an opening for a talented and energetic athletic trainer to join our team of trainers in the college’s athletic department. The Athletic Trainer is responsible for the care of student-athletes, assisting the Head Athletic Trainer in the day-to-day operation of the athletic training facility. Specific duties and responsibilities include: Athletic Training coverage for assigned team practices, home events, and travel when needed (not required). General care of student-athletes during assigned treatment hours. Maintain student-athlete medical records. Assist in the maintenance and inventory of athletic training room equipment and supplies. Potential to mentor exercise science undergraduate students who have interest in athletic training Attend all scheduled faculty and staff meetings. Other duties as assigned but not limited: scanning documents, scanning insurances, communicating with coaches, communicating with team physician/sending doc list, etc Minimum qualifications Master’s degree in Athletic Training (e.g., Athletic Training) NATABOC Certification in Good Standing State of Missouri Athletic Training licensure or eligible (Must be obtained before starting athletic training duties.) Legally eligible to work in the United States To apply, please email cover letter, resume, and contact information for three professional references to HR@moval.edu . References will not be contacted without prior knowledge and approval of candidates. Additional Information As a pre-condition of employment, the applicant must be authorized to work in the United States. Employment at MVC is contingent upon satisfactory completion of background check. Salary commensurate with education and experience. A comprehensive benefit package is available which includes medical, vision, and dental insurance; flexible spending; life insurance; retirement; holidays; sick days. Equal Opportunity Employer Missouri Valley College is an Equal Opportunity Employer and committed to a diverse and inclusive environment. Missouri Valley College does not discriminate on the grounds of color, race, sex, religion, or marital status, disability, national origin, veteran’s status, age, or sexual orientation. Employment decisions are based on qualifications, merit, and business needs. All eligible candidates are encouraged to apply. About Missouri Valley College Founded in 1889, Missouri Valley College is a private, four-year liberal arts institution located in Marshall, Missouri. Known for its diverse and student-focused environment, MVC provides an engaging educational experience that prepares graduates for meaningful careers and lifelong learning. Through innovative teaching and interdisciplinary learning, MVC empowers students to succeed in a knowledge-driven global society. Sidebar Request Information Apply to MVC Visit Missouri Valley University 500 East College Street Marshall, Missouri 65340 660-831-4000 © 2026 Missouri Valley University Plan a Visit Faculty & Staff Directory Careers & Opportunities Report a Concern/Crime/Incident Viking Shuttle & Transportation Campus Store Accreditation ADA Annual Clery Report Student Consumer Information Student Catalog and Handbook Privacy Policy Follow Us Missouri Valley on Twitter Missouri Valley on Facebook Missouri Valley on YouTube Missouri Valley on Instagram"
