    "https://www.moval.edu/about/careers-at-mvc/athletic-director/": {
      "title": "Director of Athletics",
      "description": "Director of Athletics - Missouri Valley University Skip to content Missouri Valley University Menu About About Mission, Vision, Values, and Goals God, Family, Country Our History Consumer Information Offices Leadership Careers at MVC Morris Gallery of Contemporary Art Faces of Jesus Exhibit Campus & Directions Meet Our Students & Alumni Admissions & Financial Aid Admissions & Financial Aid How to Apply Tuition & Financial Aid Scholarships Visit Missouri Valley International Students New Student Orientation Meet Our Admissions Team Payments/Policies 1098-T Information Student Employment Program Parent Resources Academics Academics Programs of Study Academic Schools Course Offerings Learning Beyond the Classroom New Student Orientation Honors College Graduate Studies MVU Online Dual Credit for High School Students Murrell Library and Academic Support Center Academic Calendar Academic Catalog Faculty Teaching Award Recipients Graduation Information Institutional Review Board Certificate Programs Student Engagement Student Engagement Activities & Events Clubs & Organizations Recreation & Fitness New Student Orientation Student Handbook Housing & Dining Health & Wellness Getting Out & About Campus Chaplain Student Employment Safety & Security Accessibility & Disability Services Student Success Center Title IX News & Events News & Events News Events Publications Social Media Alumni Alumni Homecoming Stay Connected Outstanding Alumni Alumni Recognition Center and Museum Athletic Hall of Fame Nomination Alumni Events Alumni Advisory Board Legacy Scholarship Transcript Request Viking Views Magazine Giving Viking Tailgate Zone Viking Apparel Store Athletics Search Search Search for: MyMoval Faculty & Staff Directory Pay Enrollment Fee Give to MVU Section Navigation Employment Opportunities Director of Athletics Head STUNT Coach Adjunct and Graduate Assistant Positions Head Cheer Coach Missouri Valley University | About | Employment Opportunities | Director of Athletics Director of Athletics Missouri Valley College, with one of the largest intercollegiate athletics programs in the country, seeks a Director of Athletics who is committed to long-term leadership, institutional stewardship, and legacy-building at both the college and community levels. This role is ideal for a leader who views MVC not as a stepping stone, but as a place to invest, grow, and make a lasting impact. Reporting directly to the President, the Director of Athletics provides strategic, financial, and operational leadership for an athletics department of approximately 85 coaches and staff and more than 800 student-athletes. The Director of Athletics will lead the department through a pivotal period of opportunity, while continuing to strengthen MVC Athletics as a source of pride, connection, and stability. The successful candidate will demonstrate a sustained commitment to relationship-building, program development, and the long-term success of student-athletes, staff, and the institution. Essential Functions Provide visionary, values-based leadership for all aspects of MVC’s intercollegiate athletics programs, including personnel, student-athlete success, budgeting, facilities, operations, compliance, fundraising, and community engagement. Develop and execute a long-term strategic plan for MVC Athletics that prioritizes institutional alignment, competitive excellence, fiscal responsibility, and sustained program growth. Lead the implementation and assessment of strategic recruitment plans to meet or exceed student enrollment goals Champion a culture that embraces the ideals of academic success, health, safety, and holistic development of student-athletes. Lead the department with a focus on ensuring competitive, operational, and cultural continuity during and beyond this period. Recruit, hire, support, evaluate, and retain head coaches and senior staff with an emphasis on continuity, mentorship, and professional development. Hire coaches and staff who will promote a culture of integrity and caring. Oversee and steward athletics facilities and events in a manner that enhances the student-athlete experience and community engagement. Ensure full compliance with NAIA, conference, and college policies while promoting a culture of integrity, accountability, and transparency. Lead fundraising and external engagement efforts, cultivating long-term donor relationships and strengthening community and alumni investment in the college. Actively engage with the community, donors, and alumni. Serve as the primary ambassador for Missouri Valley College Athletics locally, regionally, and nationally, fostering strong relationships with conference leadership, peer institutions, civic leaders, and community partners. Education & Experience Bachelor’s degree required; advanced degree preferred. At least five years of progressively responsible senior leadership experience, preferably with demonstrated knowledge of and engagement in NAIA athletics. Demonstrated success in recruiting, and long-term program building, organizational stability, and leadership continuity within an organization. Strategic understanding of the NAIA, including familiarity with NIL, fund raising, and student-athlete wellness. Proven ability to lead through change while maintaining institutional identity, values, and culture. Experience building, mentoring, and retaining effective administrative teams and staff. Strong financial acumen, including experience with budget oversight, strategic resource allocation, and long-range planning. Demonstrated commitment to fundraising and donor stewardship with a focus on sustained relationships rather than short-term gains. Exceptional communication, interpersonal, and public engagement skills, with the ability to build trust across campus and within the broader community. Evidence of deep appreciation for community-connected institutions and a willingness to be personally and professionally invested in Marshall and Saline County, Mo. Record of ethical leadership, integrity, and accountability. Application Instructions To apply, please email cover letter, resume, unofficial transcripts, and contact information for three professional references to hr@moval.edu . Additional Information As a pre-condition of employment, applicants must be authorized to work in the United States. Employment at Missouri Valley College is contingent upon satisfactory completion of a background check. Salary commensurate with education and experience. A comprehensive benefit package is available which includes medical, vision, and dental insurance; flexible spending; life insurance; retirement; holidays; sick days. Equal Opportunity Employer Missouri Valley College is an Equal Opportunity Employer and adheres to the Civil Rights Act of 1964, as amended, the Americans with Disabilities Act of 1990, and other legislation prohibiting discrimination in employment and access to educational programs. Employment decisions are made based on qualifications, merit, and business needs, and all eligible candidates are encouraged to apply. Sidebar Request Information Apply to MVC Visit Missouri Valley University 500 East College Street Marshall, Missouri 65340 660-831-4000 © 2026 Missouri Valley University Plan a Visit Faculty & Staff Directory Careers & Opportunities Report a Concern/Crime/Incident Viking Shuttle & Transportation Campus Store Accreditation ADA Annual Clery Report Student Consumer Information Student Catalog and Handbook Privacy Policy Follow Us Missouri Valley on Twitter Missouri Valley on Facebook Missouri Valley on YouTube Missouri Valley on Instagram"
    },
