Coach Head STUNT Coach Missouri Valley College invites applications for the position of Head STUNT Coach to lead and grow our competitive STUNT program competing in the NAIA and USA Cheer. The Head Coach will be responsible for all aspects of program management, including recruiting, practice planning, competition preparation, academic support. This role is ideal for a passionate leader who values student development, safety, and competitive excellence. The coach will collaborate and coordinate with the cheer coach, while both focus on program leadership, recruitment and retention, athlete development and safety. Key Responsibilities Plan, organize, and administer all phases of the STUNT program. Develop and implement training plans, practice schedules, and competition strategies. Foster a positive team culture emphasizing sportsmanship, academic success, and personal growth. Identify, recruit, and retain qualified student-athletes who align with MVC’s mission. Build relationships with high school and club programs. Manage recruiting databases and communications. Teach and supervise skill progressions and advanced STUNT techniques. Maintain compliance with NAIA, institutional, and safety standards. Coordinate strength & conditioning and injury prevention strategies Manage program budget, travel logistics, equipment, and scheduling. Ensure compliance with NAIA and institutional policies. Coordinate fundraising and community engagement initiatives. Required Qualifications Bachelor’s degree (Master’s preferred). Previous coaching experience in STUNT, cheerleading, or acrobatics/tumbling. Demonstrated knowledge of NAIA rules and collegiate athletics administration. Strong recruiting and communication skills. CPR/AED and First Aid certification (or ability to obtain). Commitment to student-athlete academic success and holistic development Application Instructions To apply, please email cover letter, curriculum vitae, and references to hr@moval.edu . References will not be contacted without prior knowledge and approval of candidates. Additional Information As a pre-condition of employment, the applicant must be authorized to work in the United States. Employment at MVC is contingent upon satisfactory completion of background check. Salary commensurate with education and experience. A comprehensive benefit package is available which includes medical, vision, and dental insurance; flexible spending; life insurance; retirement; holidays; sick days. Equal Opportunity Employer Missouri Valley College is an Equal Opportunity Employer and committed to a diverse and inclusive environment. Missouri Valley College does not discriminate on the grounds of color, race, sex, religion, marital status, disability, national origin, veteran’s status, age, or sexual orientation. Employment decisions are based on qualifications, merit, and business needs. All eligible candidates are encouraged to apply. About Missouri Valley College Founded in 1889, Missouri Valley College is a private, four-year liberal arts institution located in Marshall, Missouri. Known for its diverse and student-focused environment, MVC provides an engaging educational experience that prepares graduates for meaningful careers and lifelong learning. Through innovative teaching and interdisciplinary learning, MVC empowers students to succeed in a knowledge-driven global society Sidebar Request Information Apply to MVC Visit Missouri Valley University 500 East College Street Marshall, Missouri 65340 660-831-4000 © 2026 Missouri Valley University Plan a Visit Faculty & Staff Directory Careers & Opportunities Report a Concern/Crime/Incident Viking Shuttle & Transportation Campus Store Accreditation ADA Annual Clery Report Student Consumer Information Student Catalog and Handbook Privacy Policy Follow Us Missouri Valley on Twitter Missouri Valley on Facebook Missouri Valley on YouTube Missouri Valley on Instagram"
    },
