      "title": "Head Cheer Coach",
      "description": "Head Cheer Coach - Missouri Valley University Skip to content Missouri Valley University Menu About About Mission, Vision, Values, and Goals God, Family, Country Our History Consumer Information Offices Leadership Careers at MVC Morris Gallery of Contemporary Art Faces of Jesus Exhibit Campus & Directions Meet Our Students & Alumni Admissions & Financial Aid Admissions & Financial Aid How to Apply Tuition & Financial Aid Scholarships Visit Missouri Valley International Students New Student Orientation Meet Our Admissions Team Payments/Policies 1098-T Information Student Employment Program Parent Resources Academics Academics Programs of Study Academic Schools Course Offerings Learning Beyond the Classroom New Student Orientation Honors College Graduate Studies MVU Online Dual Credit for High School Students Murrell Library and Academic Support Center Academic Calendar Academic Catalog Faculty Teaching Award Recipients Graduation Information Institutional Review Board Certificate Programs Student Engagement Student Engagement Activities & Events Clubs & Organizations Recreation & Fitness New Student Orientation Student Handbook Housing & Dining Health & Wellness Getting Out & About Campus Chaplain Student Employment Safety & Security Accessibility & Disability Services Student Success Center Title IX News & Events News & Events News Events Publications Social Media Alumni Alumni Homecoming Stay Connected Outstanding Alumni Alumni Recognition Center and Museum Athletic Hall of Fame Nomination Alumni Events Alumni Advisory Board Legacy Scholarship Transcript Request Viking Views Magazine Giving Viking Tailgate Zone Viking Apparel Store Athletics Search Search Search for: MyMoval Faculty & Staff Directory Pay Enrollment Fee Give to MVU Section Navigation Employment Opportunities Director of Athletics Head STUNT Coach Adjunct and Graduate Assistant Positions Head Cheer Coach Missouri Valley University | About | Employment Opportunities | Head Cheer Coach Head Cheer Coach Missouri Valley College seeks a talented, hard-working leader to serve as its next cheer coach. The coach is responsible for leading and developing a competitive and game-day cheer program within the NAIA, UCA, and NCA. The coach promotes student-athlete success academically, athletically, and personally while representing the institution with professionalism and integrity. The coach will plan, organize, and direct all aspects of the cheer program, teaching and supervising stunts, choreography, sideline and competition routines, fostering a disciplined team culture and ensuring safety through proper training and risk management. Key Responsibilities Plan, organize, and direct all aspects of the cheer program. Meet or exceed institutional recruitment goals while Identifying, evaluating, and recruiting prospective student-athletes aligned with institutional and NAIA standards. Build relationships with high school and club cheer programs. Assist recruits through admissions and financial aid processes. Support retention and academic success of current team members Coordinate cheer participation at football, basketball, and other athletic events. Maintain compliance with NAIA and NCA rules, eligibility standards, and institutional policies. Manage team budget, travel, uniforms, and equipment. Schedule practices, competitions, and travel logistics. Required Qualifications Bachelor’s degree (required); Master’s preferred. Collegiate cheerleading and/or coaching experience. Knowledge of stunt safety, tumbling progression, and choreography. Strong leadership, communication, and organizational skills. Ability to recruit and retain student-athletes. CPR/AED and First Aid certification (or ability to obtain) Knowledge of NAIA rules and recruiting practices. Strong social media and program promotion skills. Evening and weekend travel required Ability to lift, spot, and demonstrate cheer techniques safely. Application Instructions To apply, please email cover letter, curriculum vitae, and references to hr@moval.edu . References will not be contacted without prior knowledge and approval of candidates. Additional Information As a pre-condition of employment, the applicant must be authorized to work in the United States. Employment at MVC is contingent upon satisfactory completion of background check. Salary commensurate with education and experience. A comprehensive benefit package is available which includes medical, vision, and dental insurance; flexible spending; life insurance; retirement; holidays; sick days. Equal Opportunity Employer Missouri Valley College is an Equal Opportunity Employer and committed to a diverse and inclusive environment. Missouri Valley College does not discriminate on the grounds of color, race, sex, religion, marital status, disability, national origin, veteran’s status, age, or sexual orientation. Employment decisions are based on qualifications, merit, and business needs. All eligible candidates are encouraged to apply. About Missouri Valley College Founded in 1889, Missouri Valley College is a private, four-year liberal arts institution located in Marshall, Missouri. Known for its diverse and student-focused environment, MVC provides an engaging educational experience that prepares graduates for meaningful careers and lifelong learning. Through innovative teaching and interdisciplinary learning, MVC empowers students to succeed in a knowledge-driven global society Sidebar Request Information Apply to MVC Visit Missouri Valley University 500 East College Street Marshall, Missouri 65340 660-831-4000 © 2026 Missouri Valley University Plan a Visit Faculty & Staff Directory Careers & Opportunities Report a Concern/Crime/Incident Viking Shuttle & Transportation Campus Store Accreditation ADA Annual Clery Report Student Consumer Information Student Catalog and Handbook Privacy Policy Follow Us Missouri Valley on Twitter Missouri Valley on Facebook Missouri Valley on YouTube Missouri Valley on Instagram"
